## Context
~/CNRS/code/fs-housekeeper is a git repo on branch main, clean, with an AGENTS.md and no remote. It already has pyproject.toml, uv.lock and a .venv. Its Makefile picks an interpreter with a `PYTHON :=` shell test (.venv/bin/python, else python3); three recipes run ruff, black and mypy through `uv run --isolated --with`, and two targets run `uv pip install -e`; its docs (CONTRIBUTING, INSTALL, PROJECT_OVERVIEW, QUICKSTART) say `pip install`. Observed 2026-10-23.

Practice to reach: `rules/coding-python.md` (its "Environment principles" and "Environment rules" paragraphs), tracked by 1206.

## Constraints
Closest to aligned: replace the PYTHON detection by the RUN prefix, move ruff, black and mypy into the dev group of the lock, replace `uv pip install -e` by `uv sync`, and rewrite the pip instructions in the docs.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] pyproject.toml and a committed uv.lock describe the dependencies; no hand-kept requirements.txt
- [ ] the Makefile has no PYTHON variable; recipes that run Python tools go through the `RUN` prefix
- [ ] no `pip install` in the Makefile, README or docs/
- [ ] the repo's own tests or smoke command pass from a bare shell, output quoted in the PR or log
- [ ] the alignment check of 1206 prints `ok` in ~/CNRS/code/fs-housekeeper
